From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 11:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayerVideo: a preparation keeps taking pictures from a
 full decoder

A preparation runs at speed 0. The video thread asks the decoder for a
picture after each packet it hands over, and on a queue timeout only
when not paused. Once the decoder's input is full the packet is refused,
so nothing asks any more: the decoder's pictures stay with it until it
has no buffer left, its input never drains, and the preparation waits
for a target picture that cannot come until it times out.

The MVC decoder fills its 10 MB stream buffer within a second when the
source reads fast and hands out about 17 pictures before it does, short
of a start target 0.84 s in: every 3D start fell back after five seconds.

While the gate is armed and has no candidate yet, ask on the timeout
too. The gate drops pictures before the target, which returns them to
the decoder, and stops the asking once it holds one. Nor does a source
that runs dry meanwhile turn the last dropped picture into a still frame
with a made-up timestamp, which the gate would take as its target.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayerVideo.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayerVideo.cpp
@@ -390,7 +390,8 @@
       // don't ask for a new frame if we can't deliver it to renderer
       else if ((m_speed != DVD_PLAYSPEED_PAUSE ||
                 m_processInfo.IsFrameAdvance() ||
-                m_syncState != IDVDStreamPlayer::SYNC_INSYNC) && !m_paused)
+                m_syncState != IDVDStreamPlayer::SYNC_INSYNC ||
+                PrerollSeeking()) && !m_paused)
       {
         if (ProcessDecoderOutput(frametime, pts))
         {
@@ -403,6 +404,11 @@
       if (iPriority)
         continue;
 
+      // A preparation's picture is the one the gate picks from the decoder:
+      // none is made up from a dropped one while the source catches up.
+      if (PrerollSeeking())
+        continue;
+
       //Okey, start rendering at stream fps now instead, we are likely in a stillframe
       if (!m_stalled)
       {
@@ -988,6 +994,15 @@
   }
 }
 
+bool CVideoPlayerVideo::PrerollSeeking()
+{
+  // A preparation runs paused and takes pictures up to its target only as the
+  // decoder hands them out: a decoder whose input is full gives none until asked.
+  const CVideoPrerollGate::Snapshot gate = m_renderManager.GetVideoPreroll();
+  return gate.holding && gate.armed && !gate.ready && !gate.failed &&
+         gate.generation == m_videoPrerollGeneration;
+}
+
 CVideoPlayerVideo::EOutputState CVideoPlayerVideo::OutputPicture(const VideoPicture* pPicture)
 {
   m_bAbortOutput = false;
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayerVideo.h
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayerVideo.h
@@ -98,6 +98,7 @@
   void Process() override;
 
   bool ProcessDecoderOutput(double &frametime, double &pts);
+  bool PrerollSeeking();
   void UpdatePlayerInfo();
   void SendMessageBack(const std::shared_ptr<CDVDMsg>& pMsg, int priority = 0);
   MsgQueueReturnCode GetMessage(std::shared_ptr<CDVDMsg>& pMsg,
